{
  "schema_version": "1.3.0",
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for every colour, metric and type value in the",
    "Studio interface. Nothing in views/ may write a literal colour or size;",
    "a test enforces that. Token names are chosen to read like WinUI resource",
    "keys so the same file can generate a ResourceDictionary later.",
    "",
    "SURFACES are a ladder, not a set of boxes. Depth is carried by tone and",
    "space, so a panel does not need a heavy frame to be a panel:",
    "  KcSurfaceSunken   the ground things sit in - timeline, viewport wells",
    "  KcSurfaceBase     the window itself",
    "  KcSurfaceRaised   panels, inspector, cards",
    "  KcSurfaceHeader   toolbars, table headers, tab strips",
    "  KcSurfaceControl  the things you click and type into",
    "  KcSurfaceOverlay  menus, tooltips, toasts - above everything",
    "",
    "COLOUR carries meaning, never decoration:",
    "  KcStatusRecording  red     - recording and errors, nothing else",
    "  KcStatusWarning    yellow  - warning and uncertainty, nothing else",
    "  KcStatusLive       green   - live and complete, nothing else",
    "  KcAccentPrimary    blue    - selection and focus, nothing else",
    "",
    "CLASS COLOURS are an identity, not a status. KcClassColour1..8 belong to",
    "movement classes and KcFaultColour1..6 to error classes; a class keeps",
    "its colour for the life of the project. The two sets are deliberately",
    "different families - movements cool, errors warm - so a glance separates",
    "the two kinds of interval before any label is read.",
    "",
    "ANATOMY colours belong to the athlete's own body, not to the screen.",
    "KcAnatomyRightArm/RightLeg/LeftArm/LeftLeg/Torso are resolved from the",
    "skeleton's anatomical role table, so turning the virtual camera never",
    "swaps left for right. KcAnatomyUnknown is the honest fallback for a",
    "joint whose role the skeleton format does not declare.",
    "",
    "CONTEXT colours say which editor a panel is showing: KcContextSummary",
    "neutral, KcContextMovement blue, KcContextFault coral. They are aliases",
    "of the semantic set, named for the job so a panel does not reach for a",
    "status token to mean a context."
  ],
